# Project Rules

## Stack

- ASP.NET Core 10
- C#
- PostgreSQL
- Redis
- Docker
- DDD / layered architecture
- ASP.NET Core MVC + Razor for frontend

## Architecture

- Keep business logic out of Controllers.
- Follow existing DDD boundaries and project structure.
- Domain must not depend on Infrastructure or API.
- Do not introduce a new architecture or framework unless explicitly requested.
- Reuse existing patterns before creating new abstractions.

## Frontend

- Use ASP.NET MVC + Razor Views.
- Keep UI simple and suitable for an internal news portal MVP.
- Prefer server-side rendering.
- Keep JavaScript minimal.
- Reuse existing CSS/components.
- Do not introduce React/Vue/Angular.

## Development

- Inspect existing code before implementing.
- Modify only files necessary for the task.
- Do not rewrite working code unnecessarily.
- Do not add dependencies without a clear reason.
- Follow existing naming and coding conventions.
- For large changes, explain the implementation plan before modifying code.
- Do not run the EF Core CLI (`dotnet ef`, `Add-Migration`, `Update-Database`, `Remove-Migration`). The API applies pending migrations itself on startup through `Database.Migrate()`.